    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n70738" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήρῐτος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νήριθμος</span>
			, <i>countless, immense,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ὕλη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hes.
					<u>Op.</u>
					511
				</span></i>
			: hence as pr. n. of mountain in Ithaca, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Νήριτον εἰνοσίφυλλον</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					2.632
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				9.22
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ν. ταύρων ἴχνια</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					3.1288
				</span></i>
			.</div>
